This is another reason to have ability to create custom types for MST. 
Here all we have is `private Map` and public api to interact with it.
It would be nice to make it possible to create such Type as it is done inside MST with Maps, Arrays or in some ligther way.

Imagine this as a prototype code:

```js
const setType = types.userType("Set")
    .basedOn(types.model)
    .privateProps(baseType => {
        map: types.map(baseType)
    })
    .actions(self => {
        return {
            function add(entity) {
                 if (!self.map.has(entity.id)) {
                      self.map.put(entity);
                  }
                  return self.map.get(entity.id);
            }
        };
    });
```

This is totally possible to do with simple `types.model`, but the concept is more generic and allows us to create extension types for MST and easy reuse them across community.

